<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Scandinavia and the Baltic</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of the Swedes</h1><p class="st-meta">500 CE – 970 CE (approx.) · capital Uppsala</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Early kingdom of the Svear around Lake Mälaren and Uppsala, whose kings ruled the trading town of Birka and later united the Swedish lands.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tacitus">Tacitus</a> wrote of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/svear">Suiones</a> in the 1st century, and by the 6th century the Svear had a power centre at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gamla-uppsala">Old Uppsala</a>, where great royal mounds were raised. Rich boat graves at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vendel">Vendel</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valsgarde">Valsgärde</a> show a wealthy warrior elite. Later sagas trace the kings to the legendary <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ynglings">Yngling dynasty</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Kingship was tied to the pagan cult at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uppsala">Uppsala</a>, described by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adam-of-bremen">Adam of Bremen</a>, and to assemblies of free men at the thing. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/birka">Birka</a>, founded in the 8th century on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-malaren">Lake Mälaren</a>, linked the kingdom to trade routes east to Rus' and the Byzantine and Abbasid worlds. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rimbert">Rimbert's</a> life of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ansgar">Ansgar</a> records King Björn receiving the Frankish missionary around 830 and King Olof receiving him again around 852.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eric-the-victorious">Eric the Victorious</a>, who defeated a rival at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-fyrisvellir">Fýrisvellir</a> in the 980s, and his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/olof-skotkonung">Olof Skötkonung</a> extended <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/svear">Svear</a> rule over the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/geats">Geats</a>. This union of the Svear and Götar is regarded as the start of the medieval <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-sweden">Kingdom of Sweden</a>, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uppsala">Uppsala</a> kingship gave <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a> its name.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 500 CE – 970 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Scandinavia and the Baltic</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:69.65%;width:9.35%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>500 CE – 970 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Uppsala</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Björn at Haugi, Anund, Eric the Victorious</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Norse paganism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Old Norse</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/sweden">Sweden</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Svealand, Svear kingdom, Kingdom of Uppsala</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=735&amp;focus=kingdom-of-the-swedes" aria-label="Kingdom of the Swedes on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5050 171 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of the Swedes lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5370 427L5381 440"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5381 440h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5370 427h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5370 427h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Uppsala. <a href="/atlas?year=735&amp;focus=kingdom-of-the-swedes">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
